==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
VMC (397).png|Gravikinesis
LDtTWA (372).png|Planetoid Form/Flight
VMC (404).png|Orbitakinesis
Hot Stretch (218).png|Force Field Generation
LDtTWA (442).png|Enhanced Strength
SacudidaPasado (449).png|Enhanced Durability
MA (598).png|Space Survivability
</gallery>
Gravattack can control gravity to manipulate the weight and motion of objects, allowing him to suspend and levitate targets in the air, send them flying back or forth, or slam them down to the ground with hand gestures.<ref name="AJftP" /> His control over gravity allows him to change its direction, allowing him to telekinetically send targets flying upwards<ref name="AJftP" /> or across the air as if they were falling.<ref name="FatM" />

Gravattack can increase gravity around someone and crush their body.<ref>''[[Vilgax Must Croak]]''</ref>

Gravattack can place objects into an orbital track, causing them to fly in circles at various speeds<ref>''[[The Rooters of All Evil]]''</ref>. When using his powers, he emits an aura of hazy energy{{Refn|Gravattack's gravity aura was originally colored white before being changed to green beginning in ''[[Vilgax Must Croak]]''. Meanwhile, alternate versions of Gravattack are shown generating gravity auras in different colors. For example, [[Bad Ben]]'s Gravattack generates a dark blue aura<ref name="ATTWN">''[[And Then There Were None]]''</ref> while both Negative Gravattack<ref name="FaFBM" /> and [[Weapon XI (Present)|17-year-old Weapon XI]]<ref>''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref> generate red auras.|group=note}} which he can also form into walls<ref>''[[Hot Stretch]]''</ref>, barriers and domes.<ref name="LDtTWA" />

Gravattack can use the laws of general relativity to his advantage and can reduce the speed of objects (or in some cases, creatures) to nothing even if they were moving at the speed of light before.<ref name="LDtTWA" />

Gravattack can make matter or energy orbit around him whenever he manipulates his own gravity in order to levitate and retracts his limbs, curling his body to a planetoid sphere.<ref name="AJftP" />

Gravattack possesses enhanced strength, enough to punch a hole in the ground.<ref name="LDtTWA">''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref>

Gravattack has enhanced durability, as seen when he endured physical attacks from [[Fistrick]]'s [[Class 12 Armored Mecha Suit|armor]].<ref name="AJftP">''[[A Jolt From the Past]]''</ref>

Because he is a living planetoid, Gravattack can survive in the vacuum of space.<ref name="MA">''[[Malgax Attacks]]''</ref>

Gravattack has a planetoid form where his gravitational powers are increased.

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
WYWA (310).png|Constrained by Large Size
FaFBM (289).png|Thrown Off Orbit
Hot Stretch (215).png|Unintentional Weight Damage
FAtC (257).png|Core Approaching Meltdown
LDtTWA (484).png|Black Hole Generation
</gallery>
If he takes large amounts of damage to his core, it can cause Gravattack immense pain. This will also cause him to enter meltdown and explode, which can be dangerous enough to destroy the whole area he is in.<ref name="FAtC">''[[Food Around the Corner]]''</ref>

Gravattack's large body makes it hard for him to move around in small spaces.<ref>''[[While You Were Away]]''</ref>

Sudden changes of mass can throw off Gravattack's orbit.<ref name="FaFBM">''[[For a Few Brains More]]''</ref>

Gravattack cannot stop someone from using energy-based attacks.<ref name="FatM">''[[Fight at the Museum]]''</ref>

In the presence of a deadlock with a [[Time Beast]] travelling at light speed and Gravattack trying to stop it with all his gravitational strength, he may accidentally create a black hole, with disastrous consequences.<ref name="LDtTWA" />

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*Gravattack was unlocked some time prior to ''[[Double or Nothing]]''.{{Refn|As of the events of ''[[Double or Nothing]]'', [[Albedo]] is able to transform into any alien [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] unlocked up to that episode without the need of an [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] or [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]].{{Refn|group = DJW|[[:File:Feedback's DNA Not in Alteration Field.PNG]]}} Due to Albedo being able to transform into Negative Gravattack in ''[[For a Few Brains More]]'', and [[Derrick J. Wyatt|Derrick]] being unsure how Albedo would be able to add more aliens to transform into,{{Refn|[[:File: Albedo Cannot Add More Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}} it is inferred that Gravattack was unlocked and available in the Ultimatrix prior to that episode (even though the alien itself was not conceived until '''Omniverse''' entered production). Furthermore, it is implied that Gravattack was never locked in the Omnitrix.{{Refn|http://new.spring.me/#!/DerrickJWyatt/q/3877154130763863485 (no longer accessible)|group=DJW}} Interestingly, Ben was unaware of the transformation until ''[[A Jolt From the Past]]'', when he first used it. However, Derrick later stated that his explanation of Albedo only being able to transform into aliens available up to ''Double or Nothing'' does not work due to Gravattack and that this made him unsure of Albedo's current roster,{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Retracted Double or Nothing Statement.png]]|group = DJW}} potentially assuming that Gravattack was not available during the events of ''Double or Nothing''. Given that the inference stated above reconciles the mechanism by which Albedo gained his powers and Negative Gravattack's presence, the latest statement by Derrick is ignored.|group = note|name = gravattack unlock}}

===Omniverse===
*Gravattack first appeared in ''[[A Jolt From the Past]]'', where he defeated [[Fistrick]] and saved the [[Nosedeenian|Megawhatts]] with [[Rook Blonko|Rook]]'s help.
*In ''[[Hot Stretch]]'', Gravattack attempted to battle the [[Kraaho]], but he reverted instantly.
*In ''[[Vilgax Must Croak]]'', Gravattack defeated [[Attea|General Attea]], [[SixSix (Classic)|SixSix]], [[SevenSeven]], and [[EightEight]].
*In ''[[While You Were Away]]'', Gravattack defeated [[Rick-Dan Wat-Senn|Sheriff Wat-Senn]] and [[Rook Shar]].
*In ''[[Food Around the Corner]]'', Gravattack helped negotiate a peace treaty between the [[Appoplexian (Classic)|Appoplexians]] and the [[Lewodan]]s. However, the [[Hulex]] landed on him and attempted to destroy his core to make him explode. Fortunately, he was able to revert before this could happen.
*In ''[[For a Few Brains More]]'', Gravattack was seen twice. Firstly, he broke out of the [[Proto-TRUK]] wreckage and fought [[Ultimate Albedo]] before being defeated by [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Armodrillo]]. Afterwards, Negative Gravattack briefly appeared before going [[Ultimate Gravattack|Ultimate]].
*In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', [[Bad Ben]] as Gravattack tried to capture [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] before battling [[Astrodactyl]] and [[Build-A-Guy]] until he was wiped out by the [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]].
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', Bad Ben as Gravattack was brought back to existence by No Watch Ben as [[Clockwork]].
*In ''[[The Rooters of All Evil]]'', Gravattack defeated the [[Rooters]].
*In ''[[Fight at the Museum]]'', Gravattack used his powers to keep [[Exo-Skull|Exo-Skull]] stuck in the floor.
*In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'', Gravattack argued with [[Dyno Mighty]] for not transforming him into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]] before reverting the latter into [[Ben 23]].
*In ''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]'', Gravattack chased and trapped the [[Time Beast]], accidentally creating a black hole in the process.
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', Gravattack helped [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] and [[Luhley]] escape from the [[Chimeran Hammer (Classic)|Chimeran Hammer]] and traveled back to [[Galvan Prime (Classic)|Galvan Prime]] with them.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Gravattack appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

